incident("DESIGN-AUTONOMY-SCENARIO") = {
  body: "rmw3 directed 'hagamos 1 y 2': (1) prep the autonomy guarantee (2nd-order cybernetic closed loop, precondition for vsf-rsi build), and (2) design the SCENARIO-MEMORY procedural-learning spec+plan (no code). Both produced as design artifacts, build deferred.",
  root_cause: "vsf-rsi build was gated on 'autonomy first' but no concrete certification of autonomy existed; SCENARIO-MEMORY design existed (proposals marked implemented 2026-08-26/27) but was not gate-auditable and not tied to the autonomy loop.",
  fix: "autonomy_guarantee_proposal.vsm: defines autonomy-ready via certification C1-C6 (each an ACTION/check), closed loop observe->record->evaluate->correct->watch->close, and states today's status (C1-C4 done, C5/C6 pending -> vsf-rsi still gated). scenario_memory_spec.vsm: consolidated gate-auditable spec+plan referencing existing proposals; plan('scenario-memory') added to vos_package_detailed_plans.vsm with resolvable source_spec (so G2 validates). TASKS SCENARIO-MEMORY status proposed->design (build still gated on rmw3 approval + autonomy cert).",
  lesson: "A build gated on a vague 'autonomy' is itself a memory promise. Make the gate CONCRETE: a certification checklist where each criterion is a check that fails closed. Second-order cybernetics = the watcher is watched (C1/C5). Design artifacts must be gate-auditable (a plan() with resolvable source_spec), not prose-only.",
  references: ["docs/autonomy_guarantee_proposal.vsm", "docs/scenario_memory_spec.vsm", "docs/vos_package_detailed_plans.vsm", "docs/discipline/recursive_rigor.vsm"],
}
⟦ /design_autonomy_scenario ⟧
